    "a-call-loses-its-trail--text-0": {
      "id": "a-call-loses-its-trail--text-0",
      "type": "text",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "a-call-loses-its-trail--text-0-p-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Aoyang Fang",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", Ruiyu Zhou, Xiaoying Tang, Pinjia He. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "ASE 2023",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", the 38th IEEE/ACM International Conference on Automated Software Engineering, Industry Challenge Track. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Distinguished Paper Award.",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "a-call-loses-its-trail--text-0-p-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://profile.aoyangfang.top/assets/publications/ase23/ASE_grpc.pdf",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "PDF"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " · "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://doi.org/10.1109/ASE56229.2023.00108",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "DOI 10.1109/ASE56229.2023.00108"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " · "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://github.com/CUHK-SE-Group/protoc-gen-scip",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " · "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://github.com/CUHK-SE-Group/RPCoverBenchmark",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Benchmark"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "a-call-loses-its-trail--text-0-p-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Cross-language gRPC calls can be traced from source code alone, by joining both ends of each call through the Protobuf definition they share. On DeathStarBench and the new five-language RPCoverBench, RPCover found all "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "149",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " gRPC calls (recall 100%) at 99.33% precision, without deploying anything."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "a-call-loses-its-trail--text-1": {
      "id": "a-call-loses-its-trail--text-1",
      "type": "text",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "a-call-loses-its-trail--text-1-p-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Microservices in one system are often written in different languages and call each other through gRPC. A code indexer maps calls inside one service in one language; the call that matters for the architecture, from one service into another, is where it goes blind."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "a-call-loses-its-trail--scene": {
      "id": "a-call-loses-its-trail--scene",
      "type": "component",
      "definitionId": "a-call-loses-its-trail--scene--definition",
      "parameters": {
        "scene": "trail",
        "alt": "A Go service calls a C++ service over gRPC; a single-language indexer follows the call to the Go service's edge and loses it."
      }
    },
    "tracing-waits-for-traffic--text-0": {
      "id": "tracing-waits-for-traffic--text-0",
      "type": "text",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "tracing-waits-for-traffic--text-0-p-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Both established ways to recover service dependencies work under a condition that multilingual gRPC systems break."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1-c0": {
      "id": "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1-c0",
      "type": "text",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1-c0-h-6",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dynamic: tracing"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1-c0-p-7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Logs, traces and monitoring show real traffic, but they need the services deployed and a tracing infrastructure in place, and they capture only the calls made within the observed time frame. One online service can show up to nine topologically different call graphs."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1-c1": {
      "id": "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1-c1",
      "type": "text",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1-c1-h-8",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Static: one language at a time"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1-c1-p-9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Static analysis needs no deployment, but it needs a frontend per language. gRPC calls are compiled from an interface definition into per-language code, so a single-language analyzer cannot follow a call into another service; language-agnostic ASTs (LAAST) are costly to extend because abstractions differ between languages."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1": {
      "id": "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1",
      "type": "container",
      "layout": "columns",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "children": [
        "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1-c0",
        "tracing-waits-for-traffic--columns-1-c1"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "columnWidths": [
          1,
          1
        ]
      }
    },
    "tracing-waits-for-traffic--scene": {
      "id": "tracing-waits-for-traffic--scene",
      "type": "component",
      "definitionId": "tracing-waits-for-traffic--scene--definition",
      "parameters": {
        "scene": "tracing",
        "alt": "Tracing a running system draws only the calls made inside the observed time window."
      }
    },
    "the-shared-blueprint--text-0": {
      "id": "the-shared-blueprint--text-0",
      "type": "text",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "the-shared-blueprint--text-0-p-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A gRPC service is written once in a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ".proto",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " file and compiled into bindings for every language. Inside each service an existing SCIP indexer already records two relations: the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "reference",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " from a call site to the generated client stub, and the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "implementation",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " from the server code to the generated server stub."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the-shared-blueprint--text-0-p-11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "RPCover's gRPC Matcher matches every stub to the Protobuf service and request it was generated from. Two stubs from different services that match the same service definition are joined, for example "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Conn(clientStub_go, serverStub_c++, reference)",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", and the two call graphs become one. The default matcher compares lower-cased alphanumeric names; users can plug in their own."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "the-shared-blueprint--image-1": {
      "id": "the-shared-blueprint--image-1",
      "type": "image",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "assetId": "the-shared-blueprint--image-1-asset",
      "alt": "A Protobuf Greeter service, its generated Python stubs, the server implementation and the client code",
      "caption": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "One "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "service Greeter",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "code"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ": the generated server stub is implemented, the generated client stub is referenced (paper, Fig. 3)."
        }
      ],
      "width": 80,
      "alignment": "center"
    },
    "the-shared-blueprint--scene": {
      "id": "the-shared-blueprint--scene",
      "type": "component",
      "definitionId": "the-shared-blueprint--scene--definition",
      "parameters": {
        "scene": "blueprint",
        "alt": "Both stubs are generated from one Protobuf service definition; matching each stub to it continues the call from Go into C++."
      }
    },
    "every-service-one-map--text-0": {
      "id": "every-service-one-map--text-0",
      "type": "text",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "every-service-one-map--text-0-l-12",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "every-service-one-map--text-0-li-13",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "every-service-one-map--text-0-p-14",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Index.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " An off-the-shelf SCIP indexer runs on each microservice and records its function-level dependencies."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "every-service-one-map--text-0-li-15",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "every-service-one-map--text-0-p-16",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Match.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " The gRPC Matcher reads language-neutral "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "index type",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " objects from those indexes, matches them to the "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ".proto",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "code"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " services and requests, adds the cross-service connections and merges all indexes into one SCIP index."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "every-service-one-map--text-0-li-17",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "every-service-one-map--text-0-p-18",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Convert.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " The merged index becomes LSIF for editors and graph viewers such as Memgraph."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "every-service-one-map--text-1": {
      "id": "every-service-one-map--text-1",
      "type": "text",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "every-service-one-map--text-1-p-19",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "To test this, the paper builds "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "RPCoverBench",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ": 15 services, three each in C++, Java, Python, Go and TypeScript, each acting as client, server or both, with 142 gRPC calls. Before it, no multilingual gRPC microservice benchmark existed: DeathStarBench and TrainTicket use one or two languages, and only DeathStarBench uses gRPC."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "every-service-one-map--scene": {
      "id": "every-service-one-map--scene",
      "type": "component",
      "definitionId": "every-service-one-map--scene--definition",
      "parameters": {
        "scene": "pipeline",
        "alt": "Each service is indexed by its SCIP indexer, the gRPC Matcher joins the stubs through the .proto files, and one merged index comes out as LSIF."
      }
    },
